  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 145 PM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nSaturday night through Thursday:\n\nMore uncertainty climbs into the forecast beyond the\nFriday/Saturday rain event as much depends on the interaction \nbetween the low pressure in the south central US and the high \npressure in south central Canada. In addition, where the best \nmoisture and forcing line up with respect to those interactions \nand the fact that we will be in a zonal flow regime aloft makes \nthings very uncertain. Models generally portray that same \npicture as well with differences in exactly where the precip may\nline up. Latest trends do suggest precip may sag further south\nwith primarily the southern tier of counties seeing the greatest\npotential for rain Saturday night into Sunday. \n\nAnother chance for showers and maybe weak storms Monday as a \nmore substantial shortwave swings through though moisture depth \nwill be lacking relative to the previous days and may ultimately\nimpact how much rain we actually see. While this period will\nbring rain we do not expect much instability with this overall\nand thus while embedded storms are expected, widespread\nlightning is not.  \n\nInto Tuesday, some lingering precip chances look to be possible\nas the backside of the upper level shortwave swings through but\nafter that we trend drier with higher pressure building \ndirectly over the region. With uncertainty in the earlier \nportions of the forecast comes built in uncertainty with this \nportion but models generally agree on a less active pattern for \nthe area overall. We will continue to monitor conditions as the \nupper levels will still support several systems pushing through \nits just a matter of whether the high and assumed low level dry\nair prevents much in the way of precip.\n\nKuroski",
